msgstr "Metôde (opcionel)"

#: functions/datetime.xml:19
msgid ""
"The WEEKDAY() function returns the weekday of given date. If the method is 1 "
"(default) WEEKDAY() returns 1 for sunday, 2 for monday,.. If the method is "
"2, monday is 1, tuesday 2, ... and if the method is 3 WEEKDAY() returns 0 "
"for monday, 1 for tuesday,..."
msgstr ""
"Li fonccion WEEKDAY() ritoûne li djoû d' ene date di dné. Sel metôde est 1 "
"(prémetou) WEEKDAY() ritoûne 1 pol dimegne, 2 pol londi... Sel metôde est 2, "
"li londi c' est 1, li mårdi c' est 2... Eyet sel metôde est 3, WEEKDAY() "
"ritoûne 0 pol londi, 1 pol mårdi et tchik et tchak..."

#: functions/datetime.xml:20
msgid "WEEKDAY(date; method)"
msgstr "WEEKDAY(date; metôde)"

#: functions/datetime.xml:21
msgid "WEEKDAY(\"2002-02-22\"; 2) returns 5"
msgstr "WEEKDAY(\"2002-02-22\"; 2) ritoûne 5"

#: functions/datetime.xml:30
msgid "Date1"
msgstr "Date1"

#: functions/datetime.xml:34
msgid "Date2"
msgstr "Date2"

#: functions/datetime.xml:38
msgid "Method"
msgstr "Metôde"

#: functions/datetime.xml:42
msgid ""
"The DAYS360() function returns the number of days from date1 to date2 using "
"a 360-day calendar in which all months are assumed to have 30 days. If "
"method is false (default) the US method will be used, the European otherwise."
msgstr ""
"Li fonccion DAYS360() ritoûne li nombe di djoûs del date1 al date2 e s' "
"siervant d' on  calindrî a 360 djoûs, ki tos les moes sont prins come estant "
"todi d' trinte djoûs. Sel metôde est false (fås), li metôde des Estats Unis "
"srè eployeye, ôtrumint ça srè l' uropeyinne."

#: functions/datetime.xml:43
msgid "DAYS360(date1; date2; method)"
msgstr "DAYS360(date1; date2; metôde)"

#: functions/datetime.xml:44
msgid "DAYS360(\"2/22/2002\"; \"4/21/2002\"; FALSE) returns 59"
msgstr "DAYS360(\"2/22/2002\"; \"4/21/2002\"; FALSE) ritoûne 59"

#: functions/datetime.xml:60
msgid ""
"The TIMEVALUE() function returns a number (between 0 and 1) representing the "
"time of day."
msgstr ""
"Li fonccion TIMEVALUE() ritoûne on nombe (inte 0 et 1) ki rprezinte l' eure "
"do djoû."

#: functions/datetime.xml:61
msgid "TIMEVALUE(time)"
msgstr "TIMEVALUE(eure)"

#: functions/datetime.xml:62
msgid "TIMEVALUE(\"10:05:02\") returns 0.42"
msgstr "TIMEVALUE(\"10:05:02\") ritoûne 0,42"

#: functions/datetime.xml:75
msgid ""
"The DATEVALUE function returns a number representing the day, i.e the number "
"of days elapsed since December 31, 1899."
msgstr ""
"Li fonccion DATEVALUE ritoûne on nombe riprezintant l' djoû, dj' ô bén l' "
"nombe di djoû ki s' ont passé dispoy li 31 di decimbe 1899."

#: functions/datetime.xml:76
msgid "DATEVALUE(date)"
msgstr "DATEVALUE(date)"

#: functions/datetime.xml:77
msgid "DATEVALUE(\"2/22/2002\") returns 37309"
msgstr "DATEVALUE(\"2/22/2002\") ritoûne 37309"

#: functions/datetime.xml:90 functions/datetime.xml:111
msgid "Months"
msgstr "Moes"

#: functions/datetime.xml:94
msgid ""
"The EDATE functions returns the date that is specified by a given date and a "
"number of months before or after that date."
msgstr ""
"Li fonccion EDATE ritoûne li date k' est specifieye pos ene date di dné ey "
"on nombe di moes divant ey après cisse date."

#: functions/datetime.xml:95
msgid "EDATE(date; months)"
msgstr "EDATE(date; moes)"

#: functions/datetime.xml:96
msgid "EDATE(\"2/22/2002\"; 3) returns \"5/22/2002\""
msgstr "EDATE(\"22/2/2002\"; 3) ritoûne \"22/5/2002\""

#: functions/datetime.xml:97
msgid "EDATE(\"3/31/2002\"; -1) returns \"2/28/2002\""
msgstr "EDATE(\"31/3/2002\"; -1) ritoûne \"28/2/2002\""

#: functions/datetime.xml:115
msgid ""
"The EOMONTH functions returns the last day in the month specified by a date "
"and the number of months from that date."
msgstr ""
"Li fonccion EOMONTH ritoûne li dierin djoû do moes specifyî pas ene date "
"eyet l' nombe di moes a pårti d' cisse date la."

#: functions/datetime.xml:116
msgid "EOMONTH(date; months)"
msgstr "EOMONTH(date; moes)"

#: functions/datetime.xml:117
msgid "EOMONTH(\"2/22/2002\"; 3) returns \"5/31/2002\""
msgstr "EOMONTH(\"22/2/2002\"; 3) ritoûne \"31/5/2002\""

#: functions/datetime.xml:118
msgid "EOMONTH(\"3/12/2002\"; -1) returns \"2/28/2002\""
msgstr "EOMONTH(\"12/3/2002\"; -1) ritoûne \"28/2/2002\""

#: functions/datetime.xml:119
msgid "EOMONTH(\"3/12/2002\"; 0) returns \"3/31/2002\""
msgstr "EOMONTH(\"12/3/2002\"; 0) ritoûne \"31/3/2002\""

#: functions/datetime.xml:133
msgid ""
"The YEAR functions returns the year of a date. If no parameter is specified "
"the current year gets returned."
msgstr ""
"Li fonccion YEAR ritoûne l' anêye d' ene date. S' i gn a pont d' paramete di "
"specifyî, l' anêye do moumint est rtournêye."

#: functions/datetime.xml:134
msgid "YEAR(date)"
msgstr "YEAR(date)"

#: functions/datetime.xml:135
msgid "YEAR(\"2/22/2002\") returns 2002"
msgstr "YEAR(\"22/2/2002\") ritoûne 2002"

#: functions/datetime.xml:136
msgid "YEAR(2323.1285) returns 1906"
msgstr "YEAR(2323,1285) ritoûne 1906"

#: functions/datetime.xml:150
msgid ""
"The MONTH functions returns the month of a date. If no parameter is "
"specified the current month gets returned."
msgstr ""
"Li fonccion MONTH ritoûne li moes d' ene date. S' i gn a pont d' paramete di "
"specifyî, li moes do moumint est rtourné."

#: functions/datetime.xml:151
msgid "MONTH(date)"
msgstr "MONTH(date)"

#: functions/datetime.xml:152
msgid "MONTH(\"2/22/2002\") returns 2"
msgstr "MONTH(\"22/2/2002\") ritoûne 2"

#: functions/datetime.xml:153
msgid "MONTH(2323.1285) returns 5"
msgstr "MONTH(2323,1285) ritoûne 5"

#: functions/datetime.xml:167
msgid ""
"The DAY functions returns the day of a date. If no parameter is specified "
"the current day gets returned."
msgstr ""
"Li fonccion DAY ritoûne li djoû d' ene date. S' i gn a pont d' paramete di "
"specifyî, li djoû do moumint est rtourné."

#: functions/datetime.xml:168
msgid "DAY(date)"
msgstr "DAY(date)"

#: functions/datetime.xml:169
msgid "DAY(\"2/22/2002\") returns 22"
msgstr "DAY(\"22/2/2002\") ritoûne 22"

#: functions/datetime.xml:170
msgid "DAY(2323.1285) returns 11"
msgstr "DAY(2323,1285) ritoûne 11"

#: functions/datetime.xml:184
msgid ""
"The HOUR functions returns the hour of a time. If no parameter is specified "
"the current hour gets returned."
msgstr ""
"Li fonccion HOUR ritoûne l' eure d' on tins. S' i gn a pont d' paramete di "
"specifyî, l' eure do moumint est rtournêye."

#: functions/datetime.xml:185
msgid "HOUR(time)"
msgstr "HOUR(eure)"

#: functions/datetime.xml:186
msgid "HOUR(\"22:10:12\") returns 22"
msgstr "HOUR(\"22:10:12\") ritoûne 22"

#: functions/datetime.xml:187
msgid "HOUR(0.1285) returns 3"
msgstr "HOUR(0,1285) ritoûne 3"

#: functions/datetime.xml:201
msgid ""
"The MINUTE functions returns the minutes of a time. If no parameter is "
"specified the current minute is returned."
msgstr ""
"Li fonccion MINUTE ritoûne les munutes d' on tins. S' i gn a pont d' "
"paramete di specifyî, les munutes do moumint sont rtournêyes."

#: functions/datetime.xml:202
msgid "MINUTE(time)"
msgstr "MINUTE(eure)"

#: functions/datetime.xml:203
msgid "MINUTE(\"22:10:12\") returns 10"
msgstr "MINUTE(\"22:10:12\") ritoûne 10"

#: functions/datetime.xml:204
msgid "MINUTE(0.1234) returns 57"
msgstr "MINUTE(0,1234) ritoûne 57"

#: functions/datetime.xml:218
msgid ""
"The SECOND functions returns the seconds of a time. If no parameter is "
"specified the current second is returned."
msgstr ""
"Li fonccion SECOND ritoûne les segondes d' on tins. S' i gn a pont d' "
"paramete di specifyî, les segondes do moumint sont rtournêyes."

#: functions/datetime.xml:219
msgid "SECOND(time)"
msgstr "SECOND(eure)"

#: functions/datetime.xml:220
msgid "SECOND(\"22:10:12\") returns 12"
msgstr "SECOND(\"22:10:12\") ritoûne 12"

#: functions/datetime.xml:221
msgid "SECOND(0.1234) returns 42"
msgstr "SECOND(0,1234) ritoûne 42"

#: functions/datetime.xml:231 functions/datetime.xml:254
#: functions/datetime.xml:277 functions/datetime.xml:300
msgid "First (earlier) date value"
msgstr "Prumire (li pus timpe) valixhance di date"

#: functions/datetime.xml:235 functions/datetime.xml:258
#: functions/datetime.xml:281 functions/datetime.xml:304
msgid "Second date value"
msgstr "Valixhance del deujhinme date"

#: functions/datetime.xml:239 functions/datetime.xml:262
#: functions/datetime.xml:285
msgid "Calculation mode"
msgstr "Môde di carcul"

#: functions/datetime.xml:243
msgid ""
"The WEEKS() function returns the difference between two dates in weeks.The "
"third parameter indicates the calculation mode: if the mode is 0, WEEKS() "
"returns the maximal possible number of weeks between those days. If the mode "
"is 1, it only returns the number of whole weeks in between."
msgstr ""
"Li fonccion WEEKS() ritoûne li diferince inte deus dates e samwinnes. Li "
"troejhinme paramete mostere li môde di carculaedje: sel môde est 0, WEEKS() "
"ritoûne li nombe macsimom di samwinnes possibes inte ces djoûs. Sel môde est "
"1, i n' ritoûne ki l' nombe di samwinnes etires ki s' trovèt inte di zels."

#: functions/datetime.xml:244
msgid "WEEKS(date2; date1; mode)"
msgstr "WEEKS(date2; date1; môde)"

#: functions/datetime.xml:245
msgid ""
"WEEKS(\"2002-02-18\"; \"2002-02-26\"; 0) returns 1, because there is one "
"week and 1 day in between"
msgstr ""
"WEEKS(\"18-02-2002\"; \"26-02-2002\"; 0) ritoûne 1, a cåze k' i gn a ene "
"samwinne ey on djoû inte di zels."

#: functions/datetime.xml:246
msgid ""
"WEEKS(\"2002-19-02\"; \"2002-19-02\"; 1) returns 0, because there is not a "
"whole week in between, starting at the first day of the week (monday or "
"sunday, depending on your local settings)"
msgstr ""
"WEEKS(\"02-19-2002\"; \"02-19-2002\"; 1) ritoûne 0, a cåze k' i gn a nén "
"tote ene samwinne inte di zeles, en atacant pal prumî djoû del samwinne "
"(londi ou dimegne, sorlon vos tchuzes locåles)"

#: functions/datetime.xml:266
msgid ""
"The MONTHS() function returns the difference between two dates in months.The "
"third parameter indicates the calculation mode: if the mode is 0, MONTHS() "
"returns the maximal possible number of months between those days. If the "
"mode is 1, it only returns the number of complete months in between."
msgstr ""
"Li fonccion MONTHS() ritoûne li diferince inte deus dates e moes. Li "
"troejhinme paramete mostere li môde di carculaedje: sel môde est 0, MONTHS() "
"ritoûne li nombe macsimom possibe di moes inte ces djoûs. Sel môde est 1, i "
"n' ritoûne ki l' nombe di moes etirs ki s' trovèt inte di zels."

#: functions/datetime.xml:267
msgid "MONTHS(date2; date1; mode)"
msgstr "MONTHS(date2; date1; môde)"

#: functions/datetime.xml:268
msgid ""
"MONTHS(\"2002-01-18\"; \"2002-02-26\"; 0) returns 1, because there is 1 "
"month and 8 days in between"
msgstr ""
"MONTHS(\"18-01-2002\"; \"26-02-2002)\"; 0) ritoûne 1, a cåze k' i gn a on "
"moes et 8 djoûs inte di zels."

#: functions/datetime.xml:269
msgid ""
"MONTHS(\"2002-01-19\"; \"2002-02-26\"; 1) returns 0, because there is not a "
"whole month in between, starting at the first day of the month"
msgstr ""
"MONTHS(\"19-01-2002\"; \"26-02-2002\"; 1) ritoûne 0, a cåze k' i gn a nén on "
"moes etir inte di zels, en atacant pal prumî djoû do moes."

#: functions/datetime.xml:289
msgid ""
"The YEARS() function returns the difference between two dates in years. The "
"third parameter indicates the calculation mode: if the mode is 0, YEARS() "
"returns the maximal possible number of years between those days. If the mode "
"is 1, it only returns whole years, starting at the 1st Jan and ending on the "
"31st Dec."
msgstr ""
"Li fonccion YEARS() ritoûne li diferince inte deus dates en anêyes. Li "
"troejhinme paramete mostere li môde di carculaedje: sel môde est 0, YEARS() "
"ritoûne li nombe macsimom possibe d' anêyes inte ces djoûs. Sel môde est 1, "
"i n' ritoûne ki l' nombe d' anêyes etires ki s' trovèt inte di zels."

#: functions/datetime.xml:290
msgid "YEARS(date2; date1; mode)"
msgstr "YEARS(date2; date1; môde)"

#: functions/datetime.xml:291
msgid ""
"YEARS(\"2001-02-19\"; \"2002-02-26\"; 0) returns 1, because there is one "
"year and 7 days in between"
msgstr ""
"YEARS(\"19-02-2001\"; \"26-02-2002\"; 0) ritoûne 1, a cåze k' i gn a ene "
"anêye et 7 djoûs inte di zels"

#: functions/datetime.xml:292
msgid ""
"YEARS(\"2002-02-19\"; \"2002-02-26\"; 1) returns 0, because there is not a "
"whole year in between, starting at the first day of the year"
msgstr ""
"YEARS(\"19-02-2001\"; \"26-02-2002\"; 1) ritoûne 0 a cåze k' i gn a nén ene "
"anêye etire inte di zels, en atacant pal prumî djoû d' l' anêye"

